{
  "artifact": "mindmake-approved-production-routes-r20",
  "recordedAt": "2026-09-24",
  "status": "candidate record. Owner approval for this revision is NOT recorded. Production gates have not been run against it. Do not treat it as an approval.",
  "scopeRequested": "Three instructions from Krish on 2026-09-24. (1) Remove what delays a merge to main. (2) Reword every way in so the click promises what the reader gets: the brief's questions, the brief itself, free, then a consultation and audit. (3) Build the non-duplicative sticky bar: one action, plus the offer route the reader is not already on, and never the door to the page they are standing on. The immutable approved R3 homepage is not touched, so its own \"Start here\" wording is unchanged and is the one surface still carrying it.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "Ruling (Krish, 2026-09-24): the click should promise something really good, really quickly, for free. The chain he described is the wizard, the lead capture, the output, then him getting in touch with a free consultation and audit.",
    "The label names the output, not a booking. Nothing in the flow books a session, so START_LABEL is \"Get your free AI brief\" and the consultation is named in START_SUBLABEL as what follows. This answers the item r19 held rather than shipping the wording that was held.",
    "No duration is claimed. The site states no public price or timescale and the wizard's length is not measured anywhere.",
    "The label lives in src/lib/publicLinks.ts as one constant, so the menu, the bar and every page's own close cannot drift apart. The contract tests now assert the constant rather than a literal.",
    "Two slots and never three. one-way-in permits a fork of exactly two in one control group; the door is a link and the action is a button, which is what each of them is, and links are never counted as a way in.",
    "The bar is no longer phone-only. Since the commercial surface moved to /new-age-leadership alone the shell routes have no way in of their own, and the bar already stands down whenever a page's own primary is on screen, so a wider viewport cannot produce two at once.",
    "The Decision Balance keeps its own sub-label. That surface hands the reader a decision record before the brief, which is a different and more specific promise; only its primary label is brought into line.",
    "The CI split removes waiting, not verification. No gate, engine, case count or artifact changed; two engines that were serialised now run at the same time."
  ],
